    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d946">

                <pb facs="0752" n="676" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg676"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/19854</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Canada to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-11-13T14:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 13, 1916, 2 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Down train on the Inter-Oceanic wrecked between Perone and Jalapa on the 11th,
                    cause not yet known. Vera Cruz papers admit 150 killed. Some Americans reported
                    killed or injured. Exceedingly difficult to verify. Will report names when
                    known.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canada</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
